Bit operations: 

Operator  Augmented Assignment Result
x & y     x &=y                Bitwise AND of x and y (AND)
x | y     x |=y                Bitwise nonexclusive OR of x and y (OR)
x ^ y     x ^=y                Bitwise esclusive OR of x and y (XOR)
~x        -                    Bitwise complement of x
x << n    x <<=n               Bit shift by n places to the left
x >> n    x >>=n               Bit shift by n places to the right

Bitwise AND 
The bitwise AND of two numbers is formed by linking both numbers in their binary representation bit by bit. Makes a representation of the two numbers by linking both their binary 1 

Bitwise OR 
This bitwise now takes the resulting number 1 when on both numbers theres a 1 in its binary form 

Bitwise Exclusive OR 
This bitwise takes only the binaries where they differ and a 0 where they are the same

Bitwise Complement 
Forms the one's complement of a binary number, which corresponds to the negation of all occurring bits. The actual bit operation becomes an arithmetic operation and is defined as: ~x =x-1

Bit Shift 
Used to shift the bit sequence in the binary representation, its implemented arithmetically in Python, similiar to the complement operator, A shift by x corresponds to and integer division by 2ˣ and a shift to left 
corresponds to a multiplication by 2ˣ

bit_length Method is mentioned to determine the binary representation of the integer. Ex. (36).bit_length() -- integer in () is required to Python to recognize the integer 


